        <mxCell id="g_w6fpCr9WUKTHTF8rag-242" parent="1" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;spacing=8;strokeColor=default;fontSize=12;" value="&lt;b&gt;Assumptions&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;1. Artist info is kept in the ARTIST entity (Name unique), linked by CREATED_BY (1:N). Partial on ART_OBJECTS because the artist may be unknown, so the Artist attribute was removed.&lt;br&gt;2. Type specialization is disjoint and total: every object is exactly one of PAINTING, SCULPTURE, STATUE or OTHER (OTHER catches the rest).&lt;br&gt;3. FIGURINE groups the attributes that SCULPTURE and STATUE share (Material, Height, Weight, Style).&lt;br&gt;4. Ownership specialization is disjoint and total: an object is either owned (PERMANENT_COLLECTION) or BORROWED, never both.&lt;br&gt;5. Status records whether a permanent object is OnDisplay or stored.&lt;br&gt;6. Every borrowed object comes from exactly one PROVIDER. A provider may have no current loans.&lt;br&gt;7. EXHIBITION Name is unique. Each exhibition shows at least one object; an object may never be exhibited (M:N).&lt;br&gt;8. Origin and Epoch describe the object&#39;s country/culture and are simple attributes of ART_OBJECTS." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="230" width="760" x="40" y="1100" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>
